{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_63","type":"agent_message","text":"I submitted the mitigation. It restarts the `product-catalog` deployment, which was the source of the slow requests I could find.\n\n**What I found**\n- All pods were Running, and no feature flags were enabled in `flagd`.\n- Jaeger showed `frontend-proxy` POST requests at about 1.36s, plus `product-catalog` `GetProduct` spans at 4–5s. The time was spent inside the `product-catalog` service, not in Postgres.\n- In the minute before the restart, 4 of 327 `GetProduct` calls exceeded 200ms, with a 5s maximum.\n\n**What I did**\n- Ran `kubectl rollout restart deployment/product-catalog -n astronomy-shop`. The rollout completed, and the pod is 1/1 Ready.\n- After the restart, 40 product requests and 5 recommendation requests through `frontend-proxy` all returned 200 in about 3–13ms.\n\n**Caveats**\n- I did not find a definitive root cause for the stalls. `product-catalog` logged nothing, and Postgres showed no lock contention. The container has a 64Mi memory limit with `GOMEMLIMIT=48MiB`, which is a possible cause worth checking.\n- `orders-validator` is stuck on a non-JSON record at offset 20 of the `orders-fulfillment` topic. It doesn't affect the storefront path, so I left it alone. It may need a fix or a skip.\n- The `ECONNREFUSED` errors in `frontend` logs were from 18:41:08, during the pod churn, and had stopped by the time I checked."}}
